# Run 25: ARE BOTH INSTANCES SERVING? A path-only probe of /up at 900 req/s
# over 5 generators against the two-box fleet. /up is a bare
# ActionController::Base health check: no rate limit, no cache, no Key Value,
# one trivial database round-trip — so it measures the ROUTE and the fleet,
# not the journey's work.
#
# Run 15 measured ONE box at 400 req/s clean on this exact path. Runs 21, 23
# and 24 each served ~440 req/s of Rails work whether the fleet was one box or
# two, with or without the images, with or without the page cache — which is
# either a shared-tier wall or a second instance that never took traffic.
#   * clears ~800 req/s clean  -> both instances serve; the wall is in the
#     journey's own work (database, or the Key Value rate limiter).
#   * walls at ~400 req/s      -> only one instance is in rotation and every
#     run since 22 has measured a single box.
# Scratch Key Value is pinned at 100% of 0.05 CPU during load; /up does not
# touch it, so this probe is valid even while that is being upgraded.
